\name{areg.gomp}
\alias{areg.gomp}
\title{
The \eqn{gamma}-OMP algorithm for the \eqn{alpha}-regression
}

\description{
The \eqn{gamma}-OMP algorithm for the \eqn{alpha}-regression.
}

\usage{
areg.gomp(y, x, a = 1, xstand = TRUE, sig = 0.05, R = 499, model = FALSE)
}

\arguments{
\item{y}{
The compositional responses, zero values are allowed.
}
\item{x}{
A matrix with continuous data, where the rows denote the observations and the columns are the variables.
}
\item{a}{
The value of \eqn{\alpha} for the \eqn{\alpha}-transformation.
}
\item{xstand}{
If this is TRUE the independent variables are standardised.
}
\item{sig}{
The significance level to terminate the algorithm, default value is 0.05.
}
\item{R}{
How many permutations to perform to test the significance of the candidate selected variable.
}
\item{model}{
Do you want to return the regression model with the finally selected variables?
}
}

\value{
A list including:
\item{runtime}{
The runtime of the algorithm.
}
\item{res}{
A matrix with three columns, the selected variable(s), the sum of squares of the errors in the
\eqn{\alpha}-transformed space and the p-value(s).
}
}

